Subject: [PATCH] Isolate native reply request completion and processor ownership

Apply after native patches 0001-0006 and Rezoss 0027. Extends 0004's wait
method and 0003's delivery method without changing their waits or routing.
Each result identity owns its latch, processor and memory lease. Completion
cannot signal a newer request. Scope cancellation replaces global exit/job
signals, and timeout/exception cleanup closes only owned resources. Callbacks
after cleanup are ignored. Existing register counts and labels are preserved.
Requires ReplyRequests.java from the existing generated client helper DEX.

